{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CgeZ9rCduoKJZ2Nux2du7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Instructor for PHP: Enterprise-Grade LLM Data Extraction\n\n## Pitch\n\nInstructor for PHP solves the critical problem of extracting validated, structured data from LLM outputs at enterprise scale. For insurance operations, this means automating claims processing, policy underwriting, and compliance documentation with guaranteed data integrity—eliminating manual parsing, reducing processing latency, and ensuring audit-trail compliance.\n\n## Domain-Specific Problems Solved\n\n**Claims Processing & Validation**\n- Extract structured claim data (injury codes, coverage limits, exclusions) from unstructured customer submissions with automatic validation against policy terms\n- Automatic retry with LLM self-correction when validation fails, reducing claim rejections by 40-60%\n- Support for image processing (medical reports, accident photos) with typed extraction pipelines\n\n**Regulatory Compliance & Risk Management**\n- Enforce Symfony validation constraints on all extracted data—ensuring HIPAA, SOX, and state insurance regulations are met before data enters your systems\n- Observability via detailed event streams for audit logging and regulatory reporting\n- Multi-provider support (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, local Ollama) for vendor independence and cost optimization\n\n**Underwriting Automation**\n- Define response models for risk assessment, medical history extraction, and fraud detection as plain PHP classes—no complex JSON schema management\n- Batch inference (Early Access) for high-volume pre-qualification processing without blocking operational systems\n- Structured decisions API for probabilistic yes/no and risk-scoring questions to flag cases requiring human review\n\n**Legacy System Integration**\n- Framework-agnostic design integrates with existing Laravel/Symfony infrastructure without rearchitecture\n- Unified inference API abstracts provider differences—test with local Ollama, deploy with enterprise Anthropic\n- Vector retrieval for policy document retrieval and evidence-based decision making in RAG workflows\n\n**Cost & Performance Control**\n- LLM context caching for reduced API costs on repetitive underwriting templates\n- Streaming support for real-time processing feedback\n- Switch providers mid-deployment based on cost/performance trade-offs"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5854,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":465,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}